  <h1>Representation Forcing:<br>Bottleneck-Free Unified Multimodal Models</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Traditional unified models rely on frozen, pretrained VAEs for image generation, introducing a lossy structural bottleneck. Directly generating pixels suffers from heavy structural distortions. <strong>Representation Forcing (RF)</strong> bridges this gap: by training the decoder to autoregressively predict visual representations from its own understanding encoder, UMMs acquire native structural guidance for pixel-space diffusion, matching VAE quality while improving understanding.
  </p>
