          <span id="t-val">0.00</span>
        </div>
        
        <div style="display:flex; gap:0.5rem;">
          <button class="denoise-btn active" id="btn-rf-toggle" data-rf="true">With RF</button>
          <button class="denoise-btn" id="btn-naive-toggle" data-rf="false">Naive (No RF)</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<p>
  Observe what happens when Representation Forcing is disabled: without structural anchors, the red and blue pixels mix chaotically, failing to isolate boundaries. With RF, the predicted representations act as a coordinate map, guiding the velocity vector to render sharp edges and correct geometry.
</p>
</section>

<!-- ─────────────────────────────────── §5 Design Ablations -->
<section id="s-ablations" data-code="ablations">
<div class="section-no">05 — Design Ablations</div>
<h2>Why prediction & discretization are critical</h2>
<p>
  To prove the necessity of predicting representations autoregressively as discrete tokens, the authors conducted controlled ablations on text-to-image generation (evaluated on GenEval overall score at 256 resolution).
</p>

<div class="vp">
  <div class="vp-head">
    <div class="vp-title">ablation_comparison_chart.html</div>
    <div class="vp-hint">GenEval Score vs Representation Guidance Strategy</div>
  </div>
  <div class="vp-body">
    <div class="chart-container" id="ablation-chart">
      <div class="chart-bar-row">
        <div class="chart-label">Pixel Baseline (No RF)</div>
        <div class="chart-track">
          <div class="chart-fill" data-w="25" style="background:var(--red);"><span>25%</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="chart-bar-row">
        <div class="chart-label">Continuous Regression RF</div>
        <div class="chart-track">
          <div class="chart-fill" data-w="26" style="background:var(--amber);"><span>26%</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="chart-bar-row">
        <div class="chart-label">REPA (Auxiliary Alignment)</div>
        <div class="chart-track">
          <div class="chart-fill" data-w="43" style="background:var(--border-hi);"><span>43%</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="chart-bar-row">
        <div class="chart-label">VAE Baseline (Frozen VAE)</div>
        <div class="chart-track">
          <div class="chart-fill" data-w="77" style="background:var(--muted);"><span>77%</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="chart-bar-row">
        <div class="chart-label">Discrete RF (Ours)</div>
        <div class="chart-track">
          <div class="chart-fill" data-w="76" style="background:var(--green);"><span>76%</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<p>
  The ablations reveal two core insights:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Discretization Prevents Drift:</strong> Continuous regression (predicting continuous embedding coordinates) collapses to 26% due to error accumulation in causal prediction. Discrete tokens reduce the task to robust categorical classifications.</li>
  <li><strong>Prediction Beat Alignment:</strong> REPA aligns intermediate features via loss, but fails at inference since the aligned features do not condition the output. RF places predicted representations in-context, allowing direct self-attention conditioning.</li>
</ul>
</section>

<!-- ─────────────────────────────────── §6 Experimental Payoff -->
